===== PHASE D — which classes were actually observed =====
I-provisioning-preamble
T-timestamp
PASS coverage/T-timestamp-observed (1)
PASS coverage/I-provisioning-preamble-observed (1)
Classes T and I were observed live. Class F was observed only if a live
counter moved inside this script's few-minute window; its identity across
these runs is a property of the window, not a guarantee, which is why the
rule compares that block rather than asserting it. Classes H and S cannot
be observed here — every run above is the same host and the same toolchain,
so both lines come out identical — and are exercised by the synthetic
in-position control of PHASE H2 instead.
run2 vs run3: two WARM runs minutes apart at different paths. The only
differences either carries are class T and, if a counter moved, class F.

===== PHASE E — the revision-6 defect and its cause, from committed files =====
The revision-6 evaluate.sh, recovered from git by blob id a6e6641ea13c7e4b173cf7e0932fd682f794b28d,
handed the control an ABSOLUTE path; revision 7 invokes it from inside the
work directory with a bare relative name:
PASS r6/blob-recovered (0)
PASS r6/blob-is-the-evaluation-script (1)
revision 6:
  118:"$CTL" --config "$CTLCFG" --commit-file "$WORK/upper-bad.txt" > "$WORK/wibble.txt" 2>&1
revision 7:
  125:( cd "$WORK" && "$CTL" --config "$CTLCFG" --commit-file upper-bad.txt ) > "$WORK/wibble.txt" 2>&1
PASS r6/used-the-absolute-path (1)
PASS r7/uses-a-relative-name-from-inside-the-work-directory (1)
PASS r7/absolute-form-is-gone (0)

The mechanism, driven directly: the same message file placed at two
different absolute locations, read by the same control binary, under the
revision-6 invocation form and then under the revision-7 form.
PASS mech/control-binary-present (1)
revision-6 form, location one: <scratch>/loc-one/upper-bad.txt: error Disallowed type `WIBBLE` used, please use one of ["build", "chore", "ci", "docs", "feat", "fix", "perf", "refactor", "revert", "style", "test"]
revision-6 form, location two: <scratch>/loc-two-is-a-much-longer-directory-name/upper-bad.txt: error Disallowed type `WIBBLE` used, please use one of ["build", "chore", "ci", "docs", "feat", "fix", "perf", "refactor", "revert", "style", "test"]
revision-7 form, location one: upper-bad.txt: error Disallowed type `WIBBLE` used, please use one of ["build", "chore", "ci", "docs", "feat", "fix", "perf", "refactor", "revert", "style", "test"]
revision-7 form, location two: upper-bad.txt: error Disallowed type `WIBBLE` used, please use one of ["build", "chore", "ci", "docs", "feat", "fix", "perf", "refactor", "revert", "style", "test"]
